From a75bbc156380acea726511aadd551343e822e228 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: local <local@localhost>
Date: Tue, 6 Oct 2026 11:55:24 +0530
Subject: [PATCH 04/19] Gated DeltaNet: accepted-input replay for speculative
 verify (EXL3_GDN_REPLAY)

Under speculative decoding every GDN layer keeps a recurrent-state and conv
snapshot per draft token (about 0.15 GB per draft token on a 48-layer model)
so a rejection can rewind. With EXL3_GDN_REPLAY=1 the verify forward reads the
committed state without writing it (save_state=false in the conv update and
the recurrent scan), keeps the small post-projection inputs (conv input,
post-conv qkv, beta, g), and the rewind replays only the accepted prefix.
The resulting state is bit-identical to the history path; Mamba2 layers keep
their history. -1.06 GB VRAM on Qwen3.8-27B with a 7-token DFlash2 draft.

- Graph-captured verify (EXL3_BC_GDN_REPLAY, default 1 under replay):
  BC_GatedDeltaNetSplit gets a third slot set (replay), whose mixed_qkv /
  conv_out / beta / g statics are the record. They view per-layer
  GDNReplayStorage buckets of power-of-two row counts, never reallocated, so
  captured graphs and cached replay jobs stay valid. evict() copies any record
  still pending in the storage (another cache, an abandoned verify) into a
  private eager record before the next verify overwrites it.
- batched_gdn_replay commits the accepted prefix of every layer in two
  launches per rewind (recurrent state, conv window), grouped by device and
  geometry. EXL3_BC_GDN_REPLAY=0 verifies eagerly and replays per layer.
- Two-phase rewind: every layer's record is validated and planned before
  anything runs; a commit that raises marks its records failed, so a retry
  refuses instead of advancing the state twice.
- Records die with their slot: Cache.release_state / reset and detach
  discard them (on every TP worker too), as do clear, unstash and free.
  Checkpointing a slot with an unresolved verify asserts.
- Generator: a fully accepted row that finished on EOS does not commit (its
  state is released right after).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>
